target:    tests/oracle/classify.py
gate:      composer test:classifier-plants
expect:    rule 'old-errored-registered' emits the PASS label 'a' from f.agrees()
kind:      guard-removal
rationale: Restores the hole the FIRST repair of the (a)-without-the-oracle blocker left behind,
           found by the re-attack lens and confirmed by executing the production classifier.

           The original defect was that `old-errored-registered` granted (a) — NEW PROVEN CORRECT
           — from a register hit alone. The repair added `f.agrees(f.oracle_new)`. That term is
           satisfied VACUOUSLY when NEW returned nothing and the oracle also has nothing: two
           empties compare EQUAL and always will (PITFALLS 38). So the fix closed the value case
           and left the hollow case open.

           WHY THIS RULE AND NOT ANOTHER. It sits ABOVE hollow-arms and all-hollow, so it is the
           one door into (a) that never reaches the vacuity checks. Measured on the real
           classifier: OLD errored + NEW hollow + oracle hollow returned `a`/PASS, while the
           IDENTICAL two empties with OLD hollow instead of errored returned `d-vacuous` three
           rules further down. One triple, two answers, decided by which rule saw it first — and
           the passing one was reached through the door with no vacuity check behind it.

           `oracle_class in ANSWERED` is what makes the oracle's agreement mean something: it
           must have MEASURED, not merely matched. The legitimate cases are untouched — NEW ok
           with an agreeing oracle, and NEW zero with an oracle zero, both still land on (a),
           because zero is a measurement and hollow is not.
           SUPERSEDED KILL MECHANISM, run 55: this entry's expect: used to name P45-old-errored-
           registered-needs-an-oracle-that-answered, and P45 is what killed it. It no longer gets that
           far. _assert_table_invariants() now reads each guard's bytecode at import and refuses any
           PASS-granting rule that consults f.agrees() without f.oracle_class in ANSWERED, so the gate
           dies before a plant runs. The expect: was re-pointed at the refusal - which names the RULE,
           so this entry and -02 stay distinguishable - because a mutation reported KILLED by a
           mechanism it never touched is PITFALLS 6 and the whole reason expect: exists. Consequence
           recorded rather than hidden: P45's own discriminating power is now carried by the invariant
           and by no mutation, and the plant remains as the contract's statement of the shape.
---
--- a/tests/oracle/classify.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/classify.py
@@ -329,7 +329,6 @@
         "instead of errored were called d-vacuous three rules further down — one triple, two "
         "answers, decided by which rule saw it first",
         lambda f: (f.old_class == "error" and f.register_hit is not None
-                   and f.oracle_class in ANSWERED
                    and f.agrees(f.oracle_new)),
     ),
     Rule(
